updates.txt pass 22.

A REGRESSION I COULD NOT HAVE SEEN, AND WHY.

'the bloody card won't flip' traced to setPointerCapture running on pointerdown
in OptionWheel — while a pointer is captured the browser dispatches the CLICK at
the capturing element, so every click landed on .fx-ow-track and the FlipCard
button never got one. I added that capture two passes earlier for drag
tracking.

The reason it survived: after every wheel change I verified rotate-by-scroll,
rotate-by-drag, and page-scroll-isolation, because those were what the notes had
been about. Click-to-flip was the ONE interaction I never re-checked, and it was
the only one capture could break. A component with four interactions needs all
four tested after any change to input handling, not just the ones under
discussion. That is now written into the commit as an explicit four-line check.

SECOND, A PROPERTY THAT NO PER-ITEM FUNCTION CAN HOLD.
'two of the SAME color can never be side by side' cannot be satisfied by
getTechColor(tech, index), no matter how the hash is tuned, because 'differs
from my neighbour' is a property of the SEQUENCE and the function only sees one
item. The fix had to move up a level to getTechColors(row, palette).

Worth generalising: when a requirement mentions a relationship between
neighbouring items, the code that satisfies it must be able to SEE both. If the
current function signature cannot, no amount of adjusting its internals will
work — change the signature.

Measured before changing anything: 7 adjacent clashes in 76 pairs across 19 real
rows. Measuring the old behaviour first is what turned 'this might collide
sometimes' into a number, and confirmed the fix was needed rather than
hypothetical. After: 0 in 76.

Standing: /portfolio overflows 10px at 360px from an off-screen carousel slide.
